Chapter: SPIRV Binary
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 Binary SPIR-V. Vulkan consumes a stream of 32-bit words, not the
 assembly text the disassembler emits, and this project ships no
 assembler -- so the word stream is built here, in Codex, from values,
 not by re-parsing text. Re-parsing was never an option: the text prints
 a float constant as a decimal (show over bits-to-real), which cannot be
 turned back into the exact 64-bit pattern SPIR-V stores. A word carries
 the bits; a decimal loses them.

 All opcode and enum numbers below are transcribed from the Khronos
 SPIR-V registry header (SPIRV-Headers, unified1/spirv.h), not from
 memory. With no spirv-val on the box (CLAUDE.md rule 6 forbids taking an
 outside dependency for one) the validator here shares this table, so a
 wrong number would pass our own check and still be refused by a real
 driver -- the round-trip trap. The numbers are the one thing that must
 come from the spec.

Section: Module Constants

 A SPIR-V module opens with five words: the magic number, the version
 word (0.major.minor.0 -- 1.5 for Vulkan 1.2 compute), a generator id
 (zero, we are unregistered), the id bound (one past the largest id used),
 and a schema word (zero).

  spv-magic : Integer
  spv-magic = #07230203

  spv-version : Integer
  spv-version = #00010500

  spv-generator : Integer
  spv-generator = 0

