Section: Word Encoding

 An instruction is one header word followed by its operands. The header
 packs the total word count (this header plus every operand) in the high
 16 bits and the opcode in the low 16. The two never overlap, so a
 multiply and an add place them without a shift.

  spv-instr : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-instr (opcode) (operands) =
   let wc = 1 + list-length operands
   in (wc * 65536 + opcode) :: operands

  spv-header : Integer -> List Integer
  spv-header (bound) =
   [ spv-magic, spv-version, spv-generator, bound, 0 ]

 A 64-bit literal is stored as two words, low then high. The float
 constants arrive as their raw bit pattern already, so the same split
 serves OpConstant %i64 and OpConstant %f64 -- the value is the bits.

  spv-u64-words : Integer -> List Integer
  spv-u64-words (bits) =
   [ bit-and bits #FFFFFFFF, bit-and (bit-shru bits 32) #FFFFFFFF ]

 A SPIR-V string is its UTF-8 bytes, a null, and zero padding up to a
 word boundary, packed little-endian. Our identifiers are ASCII, so a CCE
 code point converts to its byte through to-unicode.

  spv-string-words : Text -> List Integer
  spv-string-words (s) =
   let bytes = spv-str-bytes s 0 []
   in spv-pack-words (spv-pad4 (list-push bytes 0)) 0

  spv-str-bytes : Text, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-str-bytes (s) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= text-length s then acc
   else spv-str-bytes s (i + 1) (list-push acc (to-unicode (char-code (char-at s i))))

  spv-pad4 : List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-pad4 (bytes) =
   if int-mod (list-length bytes) 4 == 0 then bytes
   else spv-pad4 (list-push bytes 0)

  spv-pack-words : List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  spv-pack-words (bytes) (i) =
   if i >= list-length bytes then []
   else let w = (list-at bytes i) + (list-at bytes (i + 1)) * 256 + (list-at bytes (i + 2)) * 65536 + (list-at bytes (i + 3)) * 16777216
   in w :: spv-pack-words bytes (i + 4)

Section: Structural Validator

 The check no spirv-val on this box can do. It does not know SPIR-V
 semantics; it knows the shape a module must have: the five-word magic /
 version / bound / schema header, and an instruction stream that walks to
 the exact end, every header carrying a non-zero word count that does not
 run past the words that are there. A truncated instruction, a miscounted
 header, a lost operand -- the failures a hand-built or emitter-built word
 list actually produces -- do not survive this walk. Deeper (every id
 below the bound, types consistent) is the next rung; this is the floor.

  spv-validate : List Integer -> Text
  spv-validate (ws) =
   if list-length ws < 5 then "FAIL: header shorter than five words"
   else if (list-at ws 0) /= spv-magic then "FAIL: wrong magic number"
   else if (list-at ws 4) /= 0 then "FAIL: schema word is not zero"
   else if (list-at ws 3) <= 0 then "FAIL: id bound is not positive"
   else let s = spv-validate-stream ws 5
   in if s /= "VALID" then s
   else let s2 = spv-validate-ids ws 5 (list-at ws 3) []
   in if s2 /= "VALID" then s2
   else spv-check-refs ws 5 (spv-all-defs ws 5 [])

  spv-validate-stream : List Integer, Integer -> Text
  spv-validate-stream (ws) (p) =
   if p == list-length ws then "VALID"
   else if p > list-length ws then "FAIL: instruction runs past the stream"
   else let header = list-at ws p
   in let wc = bit-shru header 16
   in let opcode = bit-and header #FFFF
   in if wc == 0 then "FAIL: zero word count at word " & integer-to-text p
   else if p + wc > list-length ws then "FAIL: truncated instruction (opcode " & integer-to-text opcode & ") at word " & integer-to-text p
   else spv-validate-stream ws (p + wc)

 The id half: every instruction that defines a result id defines a fresh
 one, and every id is below the module's bound. Which word carries the
 result id depends on the opcode -- a type or a label names it right after
 the header, an instruction with a result type names it one word later,
 and many opcodes name none -- so the position is looked up per opcode. A
 result id at or above the bound, or a second definition of one already
 seen, is what makes a driver reject a module a shape check would pass.

  spv-result-pos : Integer -> Integer
  spv-result-pos (opcode) =
   if opcode == spv-op-type-void | opcode == spv-op-type-bool | opcode == spv-op-type-int | opcode == spv-op-type-float | opcode == spv-op-type-vector | opcode == spv-op-type-pointer | opcode == spv-op-type-function | opcode == spv-op-type-struct | opcode == spv-op-type-runtime-array | opcode == spv-op-label then 1
   else if opcode == spv-op-constant | opcode == spv-op-variable | opcode == spv-op-load | opcode == spv-op-access-chain | opcode == spv-op-function | opcode == spv-op-function-parameter | opcode == spv-op-function-call | opcode == spv-op-phi | opcode == spv-op-select | opcode == spv-op-snegate | opcode == spv-op-fnegate then 2
   else if opcode == spv-op-iadd | opcode == spv-op-fadd | opcode == spv-op-isub | opcode == spv-op-fsub | opcode == spv-op-imul | opcode == spv-op-fmul | opcode == spv-op-sdiv | opcode == spv-op-fdiv | opcode == spv-op-srem | opcode == spv-op-bitwise-or | opcode == spv-op-bitwise-and then 2
   else if opcode == spv-op-iequal | opcode == spv-op-inotequal | opcode == spv-op-sgreaterthan | opcode == spv-op-sgreaterthanequal | opcode == spv-op-slessthan | opcode == spv-op-slessthanequal then 2
   else if opcode == spv-op-fordequal | opcode == spv-op-fordnotequal | opcode == spv-op-fordlessthan | opcode == spv-op-fordgreaterthan | opcode == spv-op-fordlessthanequal | opcode == spv-op-fordgreaterthanequal then 2
   else 0

  spv-member : List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  spv-member (xs) (v) =
   spv-member-at xs v 0

  spv-member-at : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  spv-member-at (xs) (v) (i) =
   if i >= list-length xs then False
   else if (list-at xs i) == v then True
   else spv-member-at xs v (i + 1)

  spv-validate-ids : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Text
  spv-validate-ids (ws) (p) (bound) (seen) =
   if p >= list-length ws then "VALID"
   else let header = list-at ws p
   in let wc = bit-shru header 16
   in let opcode = bit-and header #FFFF
   in let pos = spv-result-pos opcode
   in if pos == 0 then spv-validate-ids ws (p + wc) bound seen
   else let id = list-at ws (p + pos)
   in if id >= bound then "FAIL: result id " & integer-to-text id & " at or above bound " & integer-to-text bound & " (word " & integer-to-text p & ")"
   else if id <= 0 then "FAIL: result id " & integer-to-text id & " is not positive (word " & integer-to-text p & ")"
   else if spv-member seen id then "FAIL: result id " & integer-to-text id & " defined twice (word " & integer-to-text p & ")"
   else spv-validate-ids ws (p + wc) bound (list-push seen id)

 The reference half: an id that is used must be defined somewhere in the
 module. Which operand words of an instruction are id references — rather
 than literals, or the result id being defined, or a string name — depends
 on the opcode, so each opcode carries a small operand model: a list of
 kinds, one per operand after the header. 0 = a literal word, 1 = an id
 reference, 2 = the result id (a definition, not a reference), 3 = the
 result-type id (a reference), 4 = the rest are id references, 5 = the rest
 are literals, 6 = a null-terminated string. Forward references are legal
 (a call names a function defined later, an entry point names its main), so
 every definition is gathered first and the references are checked against
 the whole set.

  spv-operand-kinds : Integer -> List Integer
  spv-operand-kinds (op) =
   if op == spv-op-iadd | op == spv-op-fadd | op == spv-op-isub | op == spv-op-fsub | op == spv-op-imul | op == spv-op-fmul | op == spv-op-sdiv | op == spv-op-fdiv | op == spv-op-srem | op == spv-op-bitwise-or | op == spv-op-bitwise-and | op == spv-op-iequal | op == spv-op-inotequal | op == spv-op-sgreaterthan | op == spv-op-sgreaterthanequal | op == spv-op-slessthan | op == spv-op-slessthanequal | op == spv-op-fordequal | op == spv-op-fordnotequal | op == spv-op-fordlessthan | op == spv-op-fordgreaterthan | op == spv-op-fordlessthanequal | op == spv-op-fordgreaterthanequal then [ 3, 2, 1, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-snegate | op == spv-op-fnegate | op == spv-op-uconvert then [ 3, 2, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-select then [ 3, 2, 1, 1, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-phi then [ 3, 2, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-access-chain | op == spv-op-function-call then [ 3, 2, 1, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-load then [ 3, 2, 1, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-function-parameter then [ 3, 2 ]
   else if op == spv-op-function then [ 3, 2, 0, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-variable then [ 3, 2, 0, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-constant then [ 3, 2, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-store then [ 1, 1, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-void | op == spv-op-type-bool | op == spv-op-label then [ 2 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-float then [ 2, 0 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-int then [ 2, 0, 0 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-vector then [ 2, 1, 0 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-runtime-array then [ 2, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-struct then [ 2, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-pointer then [ 2, 0, 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-type-function then [ 2, 1, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-capability then [ 0 ]
   else if op == spv-op-memory-model then [ 0, 0 ]
   else if op == spv-op-entry-point then [ 0, 1, 6, 4 ]
   else if op == spv-op-execution-mode | op == spv-op-decorate then [ 1, 0, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-member-decorate then [ 1, 0, 0, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-name then [ 1, 6 ]
   else if op == spv-op-branch | op == spv-op-return-value then [ 1 ]
   else if op == spv-op-branch-conditional then [ 1, 1, 1, 5 ]
   else if op == spv-op-selection-merge then [ 1, 0 ]
   else []

  spv-word-has-null : Integer -> Boolean
  spv-word-has-null (w) =
   (bit-and w #FF) == 0 | (bit-and (bit-shru w 8) #FF) == 0 | (bit-and (bit-shru w 16) #FF) == 0 | (bit-and (bit-shru w 24) #FF) == 0

  spv-skip-string : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spv-skip-string (ws) (p) (wc) (off) =
   if off >= wc then off
   else if spv-word-has-null (list-at ws (p + off)) then off + 1
   else spv-skip-string ws p wc (off + 1)

  spv-collect-rest-ids : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-collect-rest-ids (ws) (p) (wc) (off) (acc) =
   if off >= wc then acc
   else spv-collect-rest-ids ws p wc (off + 1) (list-push acc (list-at ws (p + off)))

  spv-op-refs : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-op-refs (ws) (p) (wc) (kinds) (ki) (off) (acc) =
   if ki >= list-length kinds then acc
   else if off >= wc then acc
   else let k = list-at kinds ki
   in if k == 3 | k == 1 then spv-op-refs ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1) (list-push acc (list-at ws (p + off)))
   else if k == 2 | k == 0 then spv-op-refs ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1) acc
   else if k == 4 then spv-collect-rest-ids ws p wc off acc
   else if k == 5 then acc
   else if k == 6 then spv-op-refs ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (spv-skip-string ws p wc off) acc
   else acc

  spv-op-def : List Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spv-op-def (ws) (p) (kinds) (ki) (off) =
   if ki >= list-length kinds then -1
   else let k = list-at kinds ki
   in if k == 2 then list-at ws (p + off)
   else if k == 4 | k == 5 | k == 6 then -1
   else spv-op-def ws p kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1)

  spv-all-defs : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spv-all-defs (ws) (p) (acc) =
   if p >= list-length ws then acc
   else let h = list-at ws p
   in let wc = bit-shru h 16
   in let op = bit-and h #FFFF
   in let d = spv-op-def ws p (spv-operand-kinds op) 0 1
   in spv-all-defs ws (p + wc) (if d >= 0 then list-push acc d else acc)

  spv-first-undefined : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spv-first-undefined (refs) (defs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length refs then -1
   else if spv-member defs (list-at refs i) then spv-first-undefined refs defs (i + 1)
   else list-at refs i

  spv-check-refs : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> Text
  spv-check-refs (ws) (p) (defs) =
   if p >= list-length ws then "VALID"
   else let h = list-at ws p
   in let wc = bit-shru h 16
   in let op = bit-and h #FFFF
   in let refs = spv-op-refs ws p wc (spv-operand-kinds op) 0 1 []
   in let bad = spv-first-undefined refs defs 0
   in if bad >= 0 then "FAIL: reference to undefined id " & integer-to-text bad & " (word " & integer-to-text p & ", opcode " & integer-to-text op & ")"
   else spv-check-refs ws (p + wc) defs

Section: Disassembler

 The text view, rendered FROM the words rather than from a second walk of
 the IR. This is what lets the text plug and the binary plug share one
 emitter: the plug emits words, and where a human-readable listing is
 wanted the words are disassembled here. Every operand is placed by the
 same per-opcode model the validator uses, so the text cannot drift from
 the binary -- it is the binary, spelled out. Ids are numbers (%7), which
 is what a module actually contains; the friendly type names the old
 emitter printed were a fiction it maintained separately.

  spv-opcode-name : Integer -> Text
  spv-opcode-name (op) =
   if op == spv-op-capability then "OpCapability"
   else if op == spv-op-memory-model then "OpMemoryModel"
   else if op == spv-op-entry-point then "OpEntryPoint"
   else if op == spv-op-execution-mode then "OpExecutionMode"
   else if op == spv-op-name then "OpName"
   else if op == spv-op-decorate then "OpDecorate"
   else if op == spv-op-member-decorate then "OpMemberDecorate"
   else if op == spv-op-type-void then "OpTypeVoid"
   else if op == spv-op-type-bool then "OpTypeBool"
   else if op == spv-op-type-int then "OpTypeInt"
   else if op == spv-op-type-float then "OpTypeFloat"
   else if op == spv-op-type-vector then "OpTypeVector"
   else if op == spv-op-type-runtime-array then "OpTypeRuntimeArray"
   else if op == spv-op-type-struct then "OpTypeStruct"
   else if op == spv-op-type-pointer then "OpTypePointer"
   else if op == spv-op-type-function then "OpTypeFunction"
   else if op == spv-op-constant then "OpConstant"
   else if op == spv-op-variable then "OpVariable"
   else if op == spv-op-load then "OpLoad"
   else if op == spv-op-store then "OpStore"
   else if op == spv-op-access-chain then "OpAccessChain"
   else if op == spv-op-function then "OpFunction"
   else if op == spv-op-function-parameter then "OpFunctionParameter"
   else if op == spv-op-function-end then "OpFunctionEnd"
   else if op == spv-op-function-call then "OpFunctionCall"
   else if op == spv-op-label then "OpLabel"
   else if op == spv-op-branch then "OpBranch"
   else if op == spv-op-branch-conditional then "OpBranchConditional"
   else if op == spv-op-selection-merge then "OpSelectionMerge"
   else if op == spv-op-phi then "OpPhi"
   else if op == spv-op-return then "OpReturn"
   else if op == spv-op-return-value then "OpReturnValue"
   else if op == spv-op-snegate then "OpSNegate"
   else if op == spv-op-fnegate then "OpFNegate"
   else if op == spv-op-uconvert then "OpUConvert"
   else if op == spv-op-iadd then "OpIAdd"
   else if op == spv-op-fadd then "OpFAdd"
   else if op == spv-op-isub then "OpISub"
   else if op == spv-op-fsub then "OpFSub"
   else if op == spv-op-imul then "OpIMul"
   else if op == spv-op-fmul then "OpFMul"
   else if op == spv-op-sdiv then "OpSDiv"
   else if op == spv-op-fdiv then "OpFDiv"
   else if op == spv-op-srem then "OpSRem"
   else if op == spv-op-bitwise-or then "OpBitwiseOr"
   else if op == spv-op-bitwise-and then "OpBitwiseAnd"
   else if op == spv-op-select then "OpSelect"
   else if op == spv-op-iequal then "OpIEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-inotequal then "OpINotEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-sgreaterthan then "OpSGreaterThan"
   else if op == spv-op-sgreaterthanequal then "OpSGreaterThanEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-slessthan then "OpSLessThan"
   else if op == spv-op-slessthanequal then "OpSLessThanEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-fordequal then "OpFOrdEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-fordnotequal then "OpFOrdNotEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-fordlessthan then "OpFOrdLessThan"
   else if op == spv-op-fordgreaterthan then "OpFOrdGreaterThan"
   else if op == spv-op-fordlessthanequal then "OpFOrdLessThanEqual"
   else if op == spv-op-fordgreaterthanequal then "OpFOrdGreaterThanEqual"
   else "Op?" & integer-to-text op

  SpvStrByte = record { text : Text, done : Boolean }

  spv-read-string-bytes : Integer, Integer, Text -> SpvStrByte
  spv-read-string-bytes (w) (k) (acc) =
   if k >= 4 then SpvStrByte { text = acc, done = False }
   else let byte = bit-and (bit-shru w (8 * k)) #FF
   in if byte == 0 then SpvStrByte { text = acc, done = True }
   else spv-read-string-bytes w (k + 1) (acc & char-to-text (code-to-char (from-unicode byte)))

  spv-read-string : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  spv-read-string (ws) (p) (wc) (off) (acc) =
   if off >= wc then acc
   else let r = spv-read-string-bytes (list-at ws (p + off)) 0 acc
   in if r.done then r.text
   else spv-read-string ws p wc (off + 1) (r.text)

  spv-disasm-rest-ids : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  spv-disasm-rest-ids (ws) (p) (wc) (off) (acc) =
   if off >= wc then acc
   else spv-disasm-rest-ids ws p wc (off + 1) (acc & " %" & integer-to-text (list-at ws (p + off)))

  spv-disasm-rest-lits : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  spv-disasm-rest-lits (ws) (p) (wc) (off) (acc) =
   if off >= wc then acc
   else spv-disasm-rest-lits ws p wc (off + 1) (acc & " " & integer-to-text (list-at ws (p + off)))

  spv-disasm-ops : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  spv-disasm-ops (ws) (p) (wc) (kinds) (ki) (off) (acc) =
   if ki >= list-length kinds then acc
   else if off >= wc then acc
   else let k = list-at kinds ki
   in if k == 3 | k == 1 then spv-disasm-ops ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1) (acc & " %" & integer-to-text (list-at ws (p + off)))
   else if k == 0 then spv-disasm-ops ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1) (acc & " " & integer-to-text (list-at ws (p + off)))
   else if k == 2 then spv-disasm-ops ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (off + 1) acc
   else if k == 4 then spv-disasm-rest-ids ws p wc off acc
   else if k == 5 then spv-disasm-rest-lits ws p wc off acc
   else if k == 6 then spv-disasm-ops ws p wc kinds (ki + 1) (spv-skip-string ws p wc off) (acc & " \"" & spv-read-string ws p wc off "" & "\"")
   else acc

  spv-disasm-instr : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  spv-disasm-instr (ws) (p) (wc) =
   let op = bit-and (list-at ws p) #FFFF
   in let kinds = spv-operand-kinds op
   in let rid = spv-op-def ws p kinds 0 1
   in let lhs = if rid >= 0 then "%" & integer-to-text rid & " = " else ""
   in lhs & spv-opcode-name op & spv-disasm-ops ws p wc kinds 0 1 "" & "\n"

  spv-disasm-loop : List Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  spv-disasm-loop (ws) (p) (acc) =
   if p >= list-length ws then acc
   else let wc = bit-shru (list-at ws p) 16
   in if wc == 0 then acc
   else spv-disasm-loop ws (p + wc) (acc & spv-disasm-instr ws p wc)

  spv-disasm : List Integer -> Text
  spv-disasm (ws) =
   if list-length ws < 5 then "; empty module\n"
   else "; SPIR-V disassembly (bound " & integer-to-text (list-at ws 3) & ")\n" & spv-disasm-loop ws 5 ""
